Subject: build(linux): use $ORIGIN for libcuemol2's install rpath

libcuemol2's INSTALL_RPATH is "@loader_path;...". @loader_path is a dyld
(macOS) token; Linux ld.so ignores it, so libcuemol2.so cannot find the
libboost_*.so.1.84.0 bundled in the same directory. On a system without
Boost 1.84 the renderer dies with "error while loading shared libraries";
with a mis-linked system Boost it dies with
"undefined symbol: ...path_algorithms21find_parent_path_size...".
(cuemol_internal.node finds libcuemol2 itself because tritium/core already
switches between @loader_path and $ORIGIN; DT_RUNPATH is not transitive.)

Pick the rpath per platform the same way tritium/core/CMakeLists.txt does.

Verified: the same CMake snippet in a standalone harness installs a library
whose RUNPATH reads "$ORIGIN:$ORIGIN/../lib/python/lib". libcuemol2 itself
was not rebuilt.

Apply with: git apply <this file>

diff --git a/src/CMakeLists.txt b/src/CMakeLists.txt
index 85fcb829..f60baa4f 100644
--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -307,9 +307,21 @@ target_include_directories(
 )
 target_link_libraries(cuemol2 PRIVATE ${CUEMOL2_LINK_LIBRARIES})
 
+# Relocatable rpath so the loader finds the shared libs bundled next to
+# libcuemol2 (Boost, Python). macOS uses @loader_path (dyld), Linux uses
+# $ORIGIN (ld.so; it does not understand @loader_path); Windows has no rpath.
+if (APPLE)
+  set(CUEMOL2_INSTALL_RPATH
+    "@loader_path;@loader_path/../lib/python/lib;@loader_path/../Resources/python/lib")
+elseif (UNIX)
+  set(CUEMOL2_INSTALL_RPATH "$ORIGIN;$ORIGIN/../lib/python/lib")
+else ()
+  set(CUEMOL2_INSTALL_RPATH "")
+endif ()
+
 set_target_properties(cuemol2 PROPERTIES
   BUILD_RPATH "${Python3_LIBRARY_DIRS}"
-  INSTALL_RPATH "@loader_path;@loader_path/../lib/python/lib;@loader_path/../Resources/python/lib"
+  INSTALL_RPATH "${CUEMOL2_INSTALL_RPATH}"
 )
 
 list(APPEND CUEMOL2_DEFS "LIBCUEMOL_EXPORTS=1")
